{"files":[{"hunks":[{"lines":[" \"\"\"OpenAI-compatible chat endpoint in front of the rollout engine."," ","-Agents (Terminus-2 through LiteLLM, our tool-calling agent) get ``http://<proxy>/s/<session_id>/v1`` as their base URL.","-Every request is turned into token ids for the session, sent to SGLang's ``/generate``, and the reply is parsed back into","-an OpenAI chat completion. When the episode is over the rollout function calls ``POST /s/<session_id>/finish`` and gets","-the slime samples of that session.","+Agents (Terminus-2 through LiteLLM, our tool-calling agent) get ``http://<proxy>/s/<session_id>/v1`` as their base URL,","+where ``<session_id>`` is the episode id.  The agent making a request identifies itself with its own session id","+(``X-Session-ID`` header and/or ``session_id`` in the body); sub-agents sharing the episode URL therefore get their","+own training rows.  Every request is rendered as SGLang's chat endpoint would render it, sent to SGLang's","+``/generate``, and the reply is parsed back into an OpenAI chat completion.  Engine-side aborts and client disconnects","+never reach the agent as finished answers and are never trained on.  When the episode is over the rollout function","+calls ``POST /s/<session_id>/finish`` and gets every agent's samples for that episode."," ","     POST /s/{sid}/v1/chat/completions   (also /v1/chat/completions with \"session_id\" in the body)","     POST /s/{sid}/finish                -> {\"samples\": [Sample.to_dict(), ...]}","     GET  /health, GET /v1/models"," \"\"\""," ","+import asyncio","+import contextlib","+import hashlib"," import json"," import logging","+import os"," import time"," import uuid"," "," from aiohttp import web"," ","-from terminal_rl.proxy.engine import EngineClient","+from terminal_rl.proxy.engine import EngineClient, EngineError"," from terminal_rl.proxy.parsing import OutputParser","-from terminal_rl.proxy.session import MessageRenderer, SessionStore","+from terminal_rl.proxy.session i